# L §4.4, §5.11 (tally 2.1.7 R3, issue #142; P32, #115): argmin gives the key least for every day the windows can
# take; q1 and q2 are both 2026-03-01, below q3's April window on every day, so they tie and ties by decides (q2);
# argmin over one window read for every key (one name) is a tie of all three, which ties by gives to q3. 2.1.6's
# refcore made both HOLE-IMPRECISE.
=== m.tally
model w
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"

index qs = [q1, q2, q3]

input w: date

input wd: date

input u: date

input cal: calendar

input d[k in qs]: date

input rank[k in qs]: int

def same: date = w

def paid: date = w + 1 day

ask a5: argmin(d[k] for k in qs) ties by rank[k], argmin(w for k in qs) ties by rank[k]

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-05) "c"
  wd = window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-01) "c"
  u = window(2026-06-06, 2026-06-07) "c"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun]) "c"
  d[q1] = 2026-03-01 "c"
  d[q2] = 2026-03-01 "c"
  d[q3] = window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-30) "c"
  rank[q1] = 2 "c"
  rank[q2] = 1 "c"
  rank[q3] = 0 "c"
=== expect a5
a5: (q2, q3)
...
